      <h3 style="font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--text); margin-bottom: 0.85rem; line-height: 1.35;">
        A free metadata remover built with true client-side security
      </h3>
      <p class="seo-text">
        Most online tools claiming to <strong>remove metadata from photos or PDFs</strong> force you to upload confidential files to third-party cloud servers. This introduces substantial security vulnerabilities: you cannot verify who inspects the server, where files are stored, or whether permanent copies are retained for surveillance or ad targeting.
      </p>
      <p class="seo-text" style="margin-top: 0.85rem;">
        Our <strong>metadata remover</strong> operates on an entirely different privacy paradigm. Utilizing high-performance client-side Web APIs (HTML5 Canvas pixel sanitization and in-memory binary sanitization), all EXIF stripping, PDF trailer reconstruction, and document sanitization executes <strong>100% locally inside your browser</strong>. Your files never leave your device, never transmit across external networks, and work completely offline once the page is loaded.
      </p>
    </div>

